# Frappe ↔ React audit

Do not audit the SPA as a generic React app. Audit it as a Frappe website page that must call TaxMate's allowlisted API.

## Skills to read first

From `~/.cursor/skills/` (Frappe) then gitignored local copies under `.cursor/skills/`:

1. `frappe-api-development` — whitelist, permissions, session vs token, structured errors
2. `frappe-app-development` — `hooks.py`, `www/`, `website_route_rules`, no `app_include_js` for SPAs
3. `frappe-frontend-development` — CSRF, same-origin, Vite proxy, login redirect. Stack here is React + `frappe-react-sdk`, not Vue/Frappe UI
4. `frappe-ui-patterns` — shell, list, form, empty/error, URL-backed filters
5. `frappe-testing` — a SPA write path without an API test is not done

Fail the audit if a finding cannot cite one of those skills plus a TaxMate file.

## Contract

`taxmate.api.get_catalog()` is the allowed surface. SPA `METHOD` / `useFrappe*` calls must map to it.

| SPA need | Required Frappe method | Forbidden substitute |
|---|---|---|
| Session / company / currency | `taxmate.api.get_session` | hardcoded AED, guessing company |
| List / get / count / search | `taxmate.api.resource.*` | raw `/api/resource` only if catalog lists the DocType; never child tables |
| Insert / save | `taxmate.api.resource.insert` / `save` | `docstatus: 1` on insert |
| Submit / cancel / amend | `taxmate.api.workflow.*` | insert with submitted docstatus |
| Party / item details | `taxmate.api.accounts.get_party_details` / `get_item_details` | `erpnext.accounts.party.*`, `erpnext.stock.get_item_details.*` |
| Make DN / SI / payment | wrap mapper then `resource.insert` (add to catalog if missing) | mapper-only `useFrappePostCall` |
| Home KPIs | `taxmate.api.dashboard.get_home` | invented tiles; missing `taxmate.api.sales_order.fulfilment_summary` |
| Desk methods | not allowed from the SPA | `frappe.desk.listview.get_group_by_count`, `frappe.desk.form.load.get_docinfo` |
| Page boot | `taxmate/www/taxmate.py` + `website_route_rules` | static `index.html`, bundle in `app_include_js` |

## Output

Group by file, `file:line`, skill cited. Mark pass only when the SPA call exists in `get_catalog()` and the Frappe method checks `has_permission` / `require_login`.
